  m_Text: 'When an email has improper grammar or punctuation there is a chance that
    the email may not be real. Words may not be spelled correctly, they may use incorrect
    punctuation, words may not be capitalized and etcetera. Official emails should
    not have this problem, if they do, they are likely a scam. For this check it
    is important to closely read the body of the email to make sure there are no
    errors. Less official emails may have some mistakes. It is important to think
    if the sender would leave mistakes in their email.

'
